Package: RII
Type: Package
Title: Relative Importance Index for Likert-Scale Survey Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Isaac", family = "Ajao",
    email = "softdataconsult@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3403-6082"))
Description: Computes the Relative Importance Index (RII), together with
    means, standard deviations and ranks, from Likert-scale survey data of
    the kind widely used in environmental, construction, engineering and
    social science research. RII is a simple 0-1 index defined as the sum
    of respondent weights divided by (highest weight x number of
    respondents); it is normally calculated by hand in a spreadsheet.
    This package computes it from raw item-level responses, ready-made
    frequency tables, or straight from an Excel, CSV or SPSS file, on any
    Likert scale range and with optional reverse-scoring of negatively-
    worded items. Real-world survey exports are handled directly: item
    columns can be auto-detected from naming conventions or from text
    Likert wording ("Strongly Agree", "Disagree", ...), even when mixed
    in with demographic or ID columns. Items are ranked automatically,
    classified into importance bands used in the literature, and rendered
    as a publication-style bar chart or a formatted Excel workbook. Two
    worked Nigerian examples are included, on construction and on
    agriculture.
